        "original_id": "5ebb1246-472e-57f4-9192-6ab225e5050d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Uri Singer, Winona Ryder, Tim Burton, Andy García, Juliette Lewis, Camilla Belle, Frank Whaley, Leighton Meester, Debra Messing, Billie Joe Armstrong, Michael Almereyda, Peter Sarsgaard, Fabio Golombek\n- Films: Open Road, Like Sunday, Like Rain, Experimenter, Beetlejuice, Man Camp\n- Companies: H2O Films, Green Apple Entertainment, VMI\n\nFacts:\n- In 1988, Winona Ryder won critical acclaim and widespread recognition for playing Lydia Deetz, a goth teenager, in Tim Burton's film Beetlejuice.\n- In August 2013, Man Camp was released after being produced by Uri Singer and Fabio Golombek and distributed by H2O Films, Green Apple Entertainment, and VMI.\n- Uri Singer has produced multiple award-winning films, including Open Road with Andy García, Juliette Lewis, and Camilla Belle.\n- Uri Singer produced Like Sunday, Like Rain, which was written and directed by Frank Whaley and starred Leighton Meester, Debra Messing, and Billie Joe Armstrong.\n- Uri Singer produced Experimenter, which was written and directed by Michael Almereyda and starred Peter Sarsgaard and Winona Ryder.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "db20e6e3-489e-5cb3-b0af-222872a4a592",
        "text": "Page: Uri Singer. Sentence: Singer has produced multiple award-winning films, among them are \"Open Road\" (Andy García, Juliette Lewis and Camilla Belle), \"Like Sunday, Like Rain\" (written and directed by Frank Whaley) with Leighton Meester, Debra Messing and Billie Joe Armstrong; \"Experimenter\" (written and directed by Michael Almereyda) with Peter Sarsgaard and Winona Ryder.\nPage: Winona Ryder. Sentence: As Lydia Deetz, a goth teenager in Tim Burton's \"Beetlejuice\" (1988), she won critical acclaim and widespread recognition.\nPage: Man Camp. Sentence: Produced by Uri Singer and Fabio Golombek and distributed by H2O FIlms and Green Apple Entertainment and VMI, Man Camp was released in August, 2013.",
